Before G01, the runner parses the fixed R2 manifest with duplicate-key
rejection; requires the exact 16 frozen record IDs and workspace-relative
paths; rejects protected or symlinked workspace inputs; and recomputes every
declared source digest through a regular no-follow file descriptor. A manifest
or source mismatch prevents every Git invocation. The later Jenn execution
decision must additionally bind the reviewed manifest SHA-256 and runner
SHA-256; this internal check does not replace that human decision surface.

## 3. Exact execution effect if later authorized

The runner's actual mode has one possible successful terminal result:

    OBJECT_ONLY_SOURCE_RUN_EVIDENCE_CANDIDATE_ONLY

It can create only its literal mode-0700 temporary root, marker, temporary
sanitized result, and one exclusive no-follow sanitized receipt. Its only Git
blob reads are seven already path-matched, replacement-disabled streams passed
directly into the in-process SHA-256 accumulator. The tree scan is name-only,
NUL-safe, in-memory, and never requests a protected object ID or protected
content.

Every other outcome is fail closed. In particular, a canonical-root symlink,
alternate object store, replacement-object setting, unknown Git command,
preexisting/symlink receipt, temporary-result mismatch, signal interruption,
missing finalizer evidence, or residue blocks the run. Catchable signals are
blocked before their temporary handlers are installed and again during cleanup,
so there is no owned-root setup or finalizer interval with an unguarded handler.
SIGKILL or process crash can never be recorded as success.

